UNIT strip
LANG rust
PRIMARY-SHA256 2749032c7a18955a230232736dc89e388f657fce21c7ee5f08b5a47f9687e5f4
SIG pub fn strip(s: &str) -> String
ABI crate shape: the artifact is a LIBRARY crate (`[lib]`, `src/lib.rs` exporting `pub fn strip`) with no dependencies —
  no main, no I/O, no binary, no regex crate. The verifier generates its own harness crate from the abstract SIG (text
  -> &str in, String out); compiling that harness against this SIG is the signature check.
ABI text = &str / String (UTF-8). Every byte of CODE (0x1B, 0x5B, 0x30..0x39, 0x6D) is ASCII, and in UTF-8 an ASCII
  byte never occurs inside a multi-byte sequence, so a byte-level scan over s.as_bytes() is exact and every kept span
  stays valid UTF-8.
ENVELOPE narrowing: text holding a lone surrogate is not representable in &str and is outside this language's envelope;
  non-text arguments (the js widening) are not representable here.
MECHANISM R1-R3 by hand, no regex: walk the bytes with an index i; when bytes[i] == 0x1B and bytes[i+1] == b'[' and
  bytes[i+2] is an ASCII digit (u8::is_ascii_digit — never char::is_numeric or is_digit on Unicode), advance j over the
  whole digit run; if bytes[j] == b'm' (lowercase only) skip to j + 1 without copying; otherwise copy the single byte
  0x1B and continue at i + 1 (the "[" and digits are then copied as ordinary bytes). Copy every other byte. Guard every
  lookahead against the end of the slice. Build the result as a Vec<u8> and convert with String::from_utf8 (it cannot
  fail, by the ABI note) or copy &str slices between codes.
MECHANISM R4: the scan never re-examines output, so a CODE formed by joining kept bytes stays (one pass, no loop to a
  fixed point).
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED bytes CODE_START = 0x1B 0x5B CITED R2 — ESC then "["; followed by one or more of 0x30..0x39 and then 0x6D
PROVENANCE colors@1.4.0 lib/colors.js (Marak/colors.js, MIT). Language file cut 2026-10-28 with the primary, before any
  blind re-emission.
